{{also|Haben}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|habēn}} < {{proto|Germanic|khaf-|lang=de}} < {{proto|Indo-European|kap-|to grasp|lang=de}}. Akin to Old Saxon {{term|hebbjan|lang=osx}}, Old Norse {{term|hafa|lang=non}} (Swedish {{term|hava|lang=sv}}/{{term|ha|lang=sv}}), Old Frisian {{term|habba}}, Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌰𐌱𐌰𐌽|tr=haban|lang=got|sc=Goth}}.  Cognate with English {{term|have}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhaːbm̩/|/ˈhaːbən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-haben.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-irregular|hat|hatte|gehabt}}

# {{transitive}} To [[have]]; to [[possess]]; to [[own]].
# {{transitive}} To [[have]]; to [[hold]]; to [[contain]].
# {{auxiliary|with a past participle|lang=de}} To [[have]]; {{non-gloss definition|forms the [[perfect tense|perfect]] and [[past perfect|past perfect tense]]}}

